{
  "_doc": "Trackpad keyboard: gesture → value per layer (bin/auxgest.h names gestures; remapd posts it, so every binding applies). LEFT HAND TYPES, RIGHT HAND NAVIGATES (2026-10-16). NO THUMBS (2026-10-17): every contact is a finger, 1–5 fingers; five's swipe up / down are spread5 / pinch5; a contact already resting (the thumb) when four fingers tap = tap5. THUMB DOWN (2026-10-18): that resting thumb (thumb-shaped by remap/thumbprint.json) with 1–4 fingers swiping up / down / left / right = thumbup1…4 / thumbdown1…4 / thumbleft1…4 / thumbright1…4 (the thumb still), tapping = thumbtap1…4; on the main pad the pointer is frozen (no moves / scrolls) while fingers are down beside it. Rolls 2–4 only. Left (aux pad): swipes type; taps 1/2/3/4 = Return / Delete / Delete Word / Escape. <hand>_nav = that hand NAVIGATING, checked before <hand>: the left pad whenever no text field has focus (one-finger swipes = arrows, three = big jumps), the right pad whenever it isn't typing (its usual state: 4/5-finger swipes, pinch/spread = app switches). Modifiers: fingers resting still on the OTHER pad: one = Shift, two = Space held (layers <hand>_one … _four win while held, then _nav, then <hand>). The right pad types (layer right) only while typing is latched on (typing.on/off). A value is a key (one character, or space/return/tab/delete/fwddelete/escape/home/end/pageup/pagedown/left/right/up/down, with optional cmd+/ctrl+/alt+/shift+/space+), a command (typing.on / typing.off / typing.toggle), a binding id from bindings.json (word.left…), tap:<chord> (posted like the tap note — Wispr Flow's ctrl+shift+f) or sh:<command>. Unmapped gestures are only logged (remapd.log 'aux'). Edited from Control Room ▸ Shortcuts ▸ Show Trackpad; remapd reloads it on change.",
